t match the calendar year requirement. I'll need to calculate the precise amount for calendar year 1981, which runs from January to December 1981. The monthly breakdown shows a clear pattern of interest payments, with significant variations throughout the year. This confirms my earlier calculation of $103,030 million as the most accurate representation of gross interest outlays for that specific period.\n\nThe terminology around interest definitions seems complex. Different budget tables might use slightly different categorizations, but the Treasury Department's \"Interest on the public debt\" appears to be the most authoritative source for gross interest calculations. I'll focus on ensuring my calculation captures the precise payment schedule.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_493d7d7798f05c1c","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\n# From FFO-3 (Budget Outlays by Agency), monthly Interest on the public debt for calendar year 1981:\nmonths = [6216, 6990, 7093, 7175, 7819, 13198, 7358, 8046, 7782, 7975, 8587, 14791]\ntotal = sum(months)\nprint('Calendar year 1981 - Interest on public debt (FFO-3):')\nprint(f'Months: {months}')\nprint(f'Total: {total} million dollars')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
